      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Choosing between an SGLT2 inhibitor and a GLP-1 receptor agonist for type 2 diabetes depends on your specific health conditions, as guidelines prioritize them based on organ protection and weight goals rather than a strict hierarchy .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "SGLT2 inhibitor",
            "link": "https://www.renalandurologynews.com/features/sglt2-vs-glp-1-individualizing-diabetes-cardiovascular-and-renal-outcomes/"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\u2705 Core Comparison for Type 2 Diabetes"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "SGLT2 inhibitors (e.g., Jardiance):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Oral pill taken once daily ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lowers A1C by up to 1%."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Best choice for heart failure or chronic kidney disease."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Side effects include genital/urinary tract infections."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "GLP-1 receptor agonists (e.g., Ozempic):",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Mostly weekly injections (though oral options exist) ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Lowers A1C by up to 1.5% to 2%."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Best choice for significant weight loss and heart attack/stroke prevention ."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Side effects include nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "\ud83d\udca1 Clinical Guidelines & Selection Strategy"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Heart Failure or Kidney Disease:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Choose an SGLT2 inhibitor first for superior renal protection and heart failure outcomes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Obesity or High Cardiovascular Risk:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Choose a GLP-1 agonist first for greater weight loss and reduced risk of major cardiac events."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cost and Administration:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Both classes can be expensive ; SGLT2 pills often have higher initial persistence than injectable GLP-1s."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your current kidney function, heart history, or whether you prefer a pill versus an injection , I can help you understand which option fits your profile better."
      }
    ],
